# =============================================================================
# What does NOT belong in this repository
# =============================================================================
# Four groups: copyrighted source material, large downloads, generated output,
# and local secrets / machine-specific files. Anyone using the repo supplies
# their own PDFs and rebuilds (see the README).

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. COPYRIGHTED SOURCE MATERIAL -- never commit any of this
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/      the textbook PDFs, ~350 MB
# sources/   the PDFs the pipelines read: textbooks, ASCO guidelines, NCCN
#            patient guides
# corpus/    ~20 million characters of text EXTRACTED from those PDFs. This is
#            the one that is easy to get wrong: it is plain .md and .jsonl, it
#            looks like project output, and it is nearly the whole of the books
#            in readable form.
# artifacts/ the indexes, which embed a verbatim copy of every chunk, plus the
#            voice cache (translations and audio) and key_state.json
data/
sources/
corpus/
artifacts/
*.pdf
*.epub

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Large downloads and archives
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights and the llama.cpp binary: multi-GB, re-downloadable with
# `bash scripts/00_fetch_models.sh`.
models/
*.gguf
*.bin
*.safetensors
# Snapshots of the whole project (these have bundled copyrighted PDFs before).
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Generated output
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
*.log

# Sarvam spend report: rewritten after every call, and its transaction list
# quotes what users asked. Rebuild any time with scripts/12_sarvam_usage.py.
sarvam_api_usage.txt

# Evaluation REPORTS are regenerated by every run and would churn on each
# commit. The question sets themselves (questions.yaml, coverage.yaml,
# patient_questions.yaml, guidance_cases.yaml) are fixtures and ARE tracked:
# they are the ground truth the numbers rest on.
eval/*.md
eval/archive/

# Design-system notes written by local design tooling.
design-system/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Secrets and machine-specific files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .env holds the API keys (Scite, Sarvam, ...). .env.example is the template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.streamlit/secrets.toml
# The self-signed HTTPS certificate ./start makes for this machine.
certs/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt

# Python
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Editors, OS, scratch
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
tmp/
.tmp/

# Claude Code agent configuration: local tooling, not part of the codebase.
.claude/
*.zip
